	"Flooded stair": ["Rough steps cut down into the rock under the copper bay, and a chain across them.", "A tag in Job's hand: 'SEALED. Not while that thing is down there.'"],
	"The Underground Lake": ["A wide, still lake under the mine. The water is black and perfectly clear, and things glow at the bottom of it.", "Every so often a ring spreads across the surface where something has come up to look at you."],
	"Old fishing camp": ["A camp from before the flood: a stove, a bench, crates of tackle gone green, a rack of old rods.", "Someone used to come down here a lot. The bench is worn smooth."],
	"Fishing spot: deep water": ["The end of the long dock. The water drops away into the dark.", "Pale cave fish turn slowly far below, the big ones keep to the deep."],
	"Fishing spot: west dock": ["The short dock. Little silver blind fish dart round the posts."],
	"Fishing spot: the shallows": ["Clear shallows over the shingle. Glow-finned fish nose about between the stones."],
	"Glow crystals": ["Crystals the colour of violets, faintly warm. They light the water round them."],
	"Fishing crates": ["Crates of hooks, line and floats, packed in rotten straw. The hooks are still sharp."],
	"Rod rack": ["Old fishing rods, bamboo and carbon fibre, a few of them still sound."],
	"Signpost: long dock, west dock, fishing camp": ["A hand-painted signpost: LONG DOCK (straight on), WEST DOCK (left), CAMP (right).", "Someone has added, underneath: MIND THE BIG ONE."],
	# Survey Level (tools/survey.py)
	"Empty display": ["An empty case with a blank label. Tar'Besh has left a card in it: 'Waiting for something wonderful.'", "Things you find on the station and in the mine could go here."],
	"Audio guide": ["A little guide terminal. Press it and Tar'Besh's recorded voice begins, very slowly, at the beginning of time."],
	"Museum catalogue": ["Tar'Besh's catalogue: every piece numbered, described and cross-referenced in three languages."],
	"Sanctum banner": ["A violet banner sewn with the Precursor diamond. The thread shines faintly in the dark."],
	"Empty crystal cradle": ["An empty cradle on a pedestal, shaped to hold a crystal. There are more of them than crystals.", "Tar'Besh believes the rest are out there somewhere."],
	"Precursor mural": ["A carved mural: a great wing spread over a world, and figures bringing crystals up from under the ground."],
	"Crystal test rig": ["An arm of probes pointed at an empty sample cradle. The readings on its screen make no sense at all."],
	"Resonance spectrometer": ["It measures the crystals' hum. The line on the screen rises and falls, slow as breathing."],
	"Research console": ["Years of measurements. One note, in S.A.R.A.'s neat type: 'They are not decaying. They are waiting.'"],
	"Measurement log": ["A log of every test run on the crystals, every one signed by Tar'Besh and countersigned by S.A.R.A."],
	"Lounge bookshelf": ["Star atlases, travel guides and a well-thumbed copy of a Paris hotel brochure."],
	"Lounge table": ["A little table with two cups and a pot of tea, still warm."],
	"Fossil of a cave crawler": ["A fossil from the moon's own caverns: something with too many legs, a very long time ago."],
	"Zaa'sh prayer bell": ["A Zaa'sh temple bell, cast in the shape of a Sky-Weaver's wing.", "Tar'Besh rings it once a year."],
	"Precursor glass shard": ["A splinter of something that grew rather than being made.", "It is warm to the touch, through the glass."],
	"Hull plate from the first crash": ["Scorched plating from the refugee transport that crash-landed here.", "Every settler signed the back of it."],
	"Terran signal codebook": ["A listening-post codebook, every page stamped TOP SECRET.", "S.A.R.A. says most of it was guesswork."],
	"Moogli trade weights": ["Brass weights from three different Moogli trading houses. None of them agree."],
	"Star map on bone": ["An ancient star chart scratched on bone. One of the stars on it no longer exists."],
	"Pirate cutlass": ["Taken from a Chernobog raider.", "The label adds, firmly: not for sale."],
	"Hologram dais": ["S.A.R.A.'s projector. The light rings turn slowly even when she is somewhere else on the station.", "Everything in this room is part of her."],
	"Station map screen": ["The whole Landing, drawn in teal light. Little dots move along the corridors: everyone, wherever they are."],
	"Concierge desk": ["A polished desk with a brass bell and a vase of real flowers.", "There is no hotel up here. There is a concierge desk anyway."],
	"Pictures of Paris": ["Two framed pictures: a lattice tower at sunset, and a cafe with a striped awning.", "A note underneath, in neat print: ONE DAY."],
	"Signal tape archive": ["Reels from the listening-post years, every one labelled and dated.", "Most of them are static. Some of them are not."],
	"Deep-space sensor read-outs": ["Dials and read-outs from the long-range sensors. One needle keeps twitching toward the same patch of sky."],
	"Memory core": ["A tall rack of humming memory. Its lights blink in a pattern, almost like breathing."],
	"Operator console": ["An operator console facing the dais. The seat is worn: people come here to talk to her."],
	"Star chart": ["A chart of the nearby stars with trade lanes drawn in. Somebody has circled a blank patch and written 'why?'"],
	"The Weaver's Wing": ["A slab of carved stone, older than the Zaa'sh calendar. It shows a great wing spreading over a burning world.", "Tar'Besh says the Zaa'sh call them the Sky-Weavers."],
	"Tar'Besh's desk": ["Catalogue cards, a magnifying glass and three cups of cold tea."],
	"Sanctum door": ["A heavy door set with violet glass. It is locked, and something behind it hums.", "Tar'Besh keeps the key."],
	"Precursor crystal": ["A crystal the size of a forearm, glowing faintly violet. It feels like it is waiting."],
	"Tar'Besh's books": ["Histories, prayer books and a well-thumbed Terran novel about knights."],
	"Panoramic window": ["The gas giant hangs over the horizon, banded blue and white, so close it fills half the window."],
	"Shuttered workshop": ["Sealed since before the refugees came. Something inside is still ticking."],
	"Telescope": ["The gas giant fills the eyepiece, blue and enormous.", "Somewhere past it, the signal is still coming."],
	"Sealed lab": ["TERRAN SIGNALS DIRECTORATE. AUTHORISED STAFF ONLY.", "The lock is still lit."],
	"Power core": ["The station's heart. It runs at a fraction of what it was built for, and it sounds tired."],
	"The Harbinger": ["Something vast rises out of the black water, older than the station and maybe older than the moon.", "It has not noticed you. Yet."],
	"Underground ocean": ["Warm, dark water as far as the lamp reaches. Zaas would weep.", "Somewhere out there, the Harbinger is waiting."],
	"Barricade": ["Planks, hull plate and a lot of bolts. Past it the tunnel drops into the dark.", "Something down there is scratching."],
	"Villa door": ["Locked. Whoever built a private villa out here did not leave a forwarding address."],
	"Herb beds": ["Evarra's herbs, under the one small dome on the Landing that holds air, water and light. It smells green here."],
	"Fountain": ["The officers' fountain. Zaas runs the station's reclaimed water through it now, and someone has planted the centrepiece.", "It is the closest thing the Landing has to a town square."],
	"Notice board": ["WANTED: coil wire, any length. - Tikka", "LOST: one left boot, sentimental value. FOUND: one ocean (pending). - Z."],
	"Market stall": ["A stall under a striped awning. Nobody is selling today, but the crates are full."],
	"Star dome": ["An old telescope under clear glass. The gas giant takes up half the sky."],
	"Locked apartment": ["Private quarters, shuttered. Guests could stay here one day, if anyone could find the keys."],
	"Hotel desk": ["The duty officer's desk. Dust it off, add a bell, and it is a front desk."],
	"Abandoned shop": ["A shop front, shuttered. The sign has been painted over twice in two different alphabets."],
	"Half-built chair": ["Steel legs, a plastic seat, and a pencil note: 'IMAGINE THIS IN OAK.'"],
	"Weapon racks": ["Spears, blades, two dented helmets and a clipboard. Everything has a tag. Everything is signed for."],
	"Airlock": ["The outer door is sealed and the light above it is red.", "Sara: The pad is in hard vacuum. When you have a suit that holds air, I will open it. Not before."],
	"Customs gate": ["A customs gate for a port that has never had a visitor. The stamp pad is still wet. Sara keeps it that way."],
	"Old drill hall": ["A parade floor the garrison never marched on. It is the biggest empty room on the Landing.", "A hotel could use a room like this."],
	"Dry ponds": ["Cracked basins under broken glass. Somebody built fish ponds here, and a path to walk around them.", "With water and a roof it would be the prettiest place on the moon."],
	"Workbench": ["A workbench, a vice, and a wall of empty hooks. Sara says the room is yours if you can find a use for it."],
	"Air reclaimer": ["Rows of scrubbers, breathing for the whole station. Half of them rattle.", "Merrow has chalked a number on each one. The low numbers are the ones she trusts."],
	"East airlock": ["A maintenance airlock. The outer door is sealed and the light above it is red.", "Past it is bare rock. You would need a suit."],
	"Medbay beds": ["Three beds, clean sheets, and a chart on each. Two of the charts say JOB."],
	"Loom": ["Sesska's loom. It has more moving parts than your ship, and all of them work."],
	"Broken agri dome": ["Cracked panels, dry soil, dead machines. It was built to feed a garrison.", "With glass and water this could feed the whole Landing."],
	"Old bunks": ["Rows of bunks for soldiers who never came. Clear out the rubble and these would be guest rooms."],
	"Library shelves": ["Field manuals, mostly. Someone has added cookbooks, a few novels and a children's atlas of Earth."],
	"Landing pad": ["Through the airlock window: painted lines on bare rock, for a spaceport that was never finished.", "One day ships will set down there."],
	# Homes (tools/residences.py, tools/east.py, tools/caves.py), 20 Nov. Claude's placeholder lines.
	"Bram's bed": ["A short, wide Moogli bed, made with military corners. A price tag is still stuck to the headboard."],
	"Bram's ledgers": ["Every trade Bram has made since he landed, in tiny, careful handwriting.", "One page is just the word 'NO' and a date."],
	"Bram's strongbox": ["Locked, then locked again, then tied shut with wire. Bram trusts boxes more than banks."],
	"Salvage crate": ["Bits Bram hasn't priced yet. A note on top says DO NOT TOUCH (THIS MEANS JOB)."],
	"Freya's bed": ["The blanket has scorch marks. So does the pillow."],
	"Freya's bench": ["A half-stripped thruster valve, laid out part by part on a rag in the order it came apart."],
	"Ship schematics": ["Hull drawings for the fighter in the bay, scribbled over in three colours of pen."],
	"Job's bed": ["A big, plain bed, made in a hurry. His hard hat hangs on the post."],
	"Job's weights": ["Plates of scrap hull, welded onto a bar. Heavier than they look. They look very heavy."],
	"Box of geodes": ["Geodes Job hasn't cracked yet. He's saving the best-sounding ones for a special day."],
	"Zaas's bed": ["The sheets are printed with waves. There is a towel folded on the end, just in case."],
	"Zaas's telescope": ["Pointed at the gas giant. A note taped to it says: 'Clouds? Or oceans?? CHECK AGAIN.'"],
	"Zaas's ocean charts": ["Charts of every moon in the system, with blue circled wherever there might be water. There is a lot of blue."],
	"Fish tank": ["A full, bubbling tank with plants, gravel and a little castle. No fish. Zaas says it's ready for when he finds some."],
	"Jasper's bed": ["Neatly made. A folded apron lies on the pillow, ready for the morning."],
	"Jasper's cookbooks": ["Old Earth cookbooks, splattered and annotated. Every margin says 'more butter'."],
	"Jasper's pictures of Paris": ["Postcards of a city Jasper has never seen: cafés, bridges, a tower of iron lace."],
	"Jasper's range": ["Jasper's pride: a home stove tuned well past its rating. Every pan has its own hook."],
	"Spice rack": ["Jars labelled in Jasper's hand. Half the spices are Evarra's herbs, renamed."],
	"Evarra's bed": ["Pressed flowers are tucked under the pillow. The room smells of lavender."],
	"Evarra's flower box": ["Flowers in every colour the Landing has. Evarra talks to them in the mornings."],
	"Drying herbs": ["Bundles of herbs hung upside down to dry: mint, sage and something blue that hums faintly."],
	"Evarra's herb bed": ["A long planter of kitchen herbs, where Jasper can reach them without asking. He asks anyway."],
	"Family screen": ["A big screen for the evenings. Someone has left it paused on a cooking show."],
	"Maren and Owen's bed": ["A quilt sewn from thirty years of ports: a square of cloth from every place they lived."],
	"Owen's bedside books": ["A stack of codexes with bookmarks in all of them. Owen reads five at once."],
	"Pip's bed": ["Unmade. There is a torch under the pillow, and a map under the torch."],
	"Pip's map of the station": ["Pip's own map of the Landing, with secret routes marked in red. Several say 'NOT ALLOWED (YET)'."],
	"Pip's schoolbooks": ["Owen's lessons, copied out by hand. The margins are full of drawings of rockets."],
	"Pip's toy chest": ["Toys, rocks, a broken drone and a sock that may be a puppet."],
	"Pip's play set": ["A little climbing frame. Pip says it's a training rig for the mine."],
	"Pip's holo-game": ["A glowing board game. Pip has written his own rules on a card beside it. He always wins."],
	"Family bookshelf": ["Picture books for Pip, medical texts for Maren and, for Owen, everything else."],
	"Owen's desk": ["Notes on the codexes he's collecting, cross-referenced and tied with string."],
	"Owen's codex collection": ["Codexes from all over the station. Each one tells a little more of the Landing's story."],
	"Codex under glass": ["Owen's rarest codex, under glass. The label says: 'Please ask before breathing on it.'"],
	"Library overflow": ["Books that didn't fit in the library. Owen calls it 'temporary'. It has been here two years."],
	"Spare cot": ["A clean cot for patients who need watching overnight. Maren never quite stops being a doctor."],
	"Maren's medical terminal": ["Maren's records, and a long list of reminders for everyone on the station."],
	"Maren's medicine cabinet": ["Neat rows of bottles, each one labelled twice. A sticker says: PIP, NO."],
	"Garrick and Saffi's bed": ["A sturdy bed. Garrick's side is very tidy. Saffi's side has a novel and a fox-tail brush."],
	"Garrick's uniform locker": ["Three uniforms, pressed. A list of who has signed for what is taped inside the door."],
	"Saffi's plants": ["Saffi's houseplants, each with a name tag. She says they behave better than Kit."],
	"Garrick's training bag": ["A heavy bag, patched many times. Garrick says it keeps him calm. The bag disagrees."],
	"Kit's bed": ["Covered in drawings of ships. One of them has 'KIT, CAPTAIN' painted on the side."],
	"Kit's telescope": ["Kit's telescope, aimed at the dark between the stars. He watches for lights that shouldn't be there."],
	"Kit's sky chart": ["Kit's own star chart. Some of the stars are labelled 'MINE'."],
	"Kit's toy chest": ["Toy blasters, a stuffed lizard and a badge that says DEPUTY."],
	"Kit's toys": ["A climbing frame Kit uses as a lookout tower."],
	"Kit's holo-game": ["A glowing game board. The scores show Kit just ahead of Pip, by one."],
	"Tobbin and Merrow's bed": ["A low, round Moogli bed that Tobbin built himself. He wishes it were wood."],
	"Tobbin's wardrobe": ["Tobbin built this too. Steel and plastic, carved to look like wood grain. Almost."],
	"Tobbin's furniture blueprints": ["Designs for chairs, tables and cribs, all marked 'OAK' and then crossed out."],
	"Merrow's seedlings": ["Seed trays, each labelled and dated. Merrow is starting next season's crops at home."],
	"Merrow's grow bed": ["A small hydroponic bed of greens for the family table. It runs better than the fountain."],
	"Merrow's water filter": ["A home-built water filter. Merrow has tuned it so well the water tastes of nothing at all."],
	"Tobbin's home bench": ["Half a chair, a jar of screws and a pencil drawing of a tree."],
	"Nub's bed": ["A little bed shaped like a lily pad. Tobbin's work, and Nub's idea."],
	"Nub's drawing desk": ["Crayons, pencils and a stack of Tobbin's old blueprints, every one drawn on."],
	"Nub's drawings": ["Nub's drawings: Tobbin, Merrow, a very big frog-shaped ship, and you."],
	"Nub's toy chest": ["Blocks, a whistle and a toy hammer that Tobbin says is 'for later'."],
	"Nub's toys": ["A climbing frame. Nub has tied a flag to the top."],
	"Quill's bed": ["Made so tightly you could bounce a coin on it. His glasses case sits on the shelf, open and waiting."],
	"Quill's medical journals": ["Old medical journals, shelved by date. Quill reads them in the evenings and corrects them in pencil."],
	"Quill's desk": ["Pens in a row, by length. A label maker. Labels on the label maker."],
	"Pressed ferns": ["Ferns pressed flat under glass, from the Agri dome. Each has its Latin name written beneath it."],
	"Ix'ali's bed": ["A low Zaa'sh bed. A practice blade is tucked within reach of the pillow."],
	"Ix'ali's human weapons": ["Human weapons in a case: a dented sabre, a flare gun, a kitchen knife labelled 'probably a weapon'."],
	"Practice dummy": ["A training dummy, battered flat on one side. Someone has drawn a pirate's hat on it."],
	"Practice blades": ["A rack of blunted practice blades. Ix'ali keeps them sharper than she should."],
	"Tar'Besh's bed": ["A plain bed. A prayer cord hangs from the post, worn smooth."],
	"Tar'Besh's prayer garden": ["A small garden of pale moss and stones, raked into the shape of a wing."],
	"Tar'Besh's writing desk": ["Notes for the museum, written very slowly and very beautifully."],
	"Sky-Weaver banner": ["A Zaa'sh banner with the Sky-Weaver's wing stitched in silver thread."],
	"Shared bookshelf": ["Medical texts, Zaa'sh scripture, and a weapons catalogue. Nobody admits which is whose."],
	"Chess set": ["A game in progress. Someone has left a note under the board: 'Your move, Tar'Besh. - Q.'"],
	"Artie's bed": ["Made with hospital corners, the way the Scouts taught him. A neckerchief is folded on the pillow."],
	"Artie's knot board": ["A board of knots, each one labelled: reef, bowline, sheet bend. He ties them when he can't sleep."],
	"Artie's library books": ["Library books about the last few centuries, all overdue. Owen hasn't the heart to ask for them back."],
	"Stu's bed": ["A small Moogli bed. Under it is the crate he stowed away in, kept for luck."],
	"The hydroponics crate": ["The crate Stu stowed away in. It still smells of lettuce."],
	"Stu's luggage cart": ["A hotel luggage cart, polished to a shine. Stu says he's just borrowing it."],
	"Ana's bed": ["A narrow bed, made fast and neat, like a bunk on a ship."],
	"Ana's flight charts": ["Flight charts of the system, with old pirate routes marked in red and then crossed out."],
	"Ana's nav console": ["A nav console she built from spares. It's already plotting a course somewhere."],
	"Tikka and Sesska's bed": ["A wide, round Arachnay bed, hung with silk. Forty years of marriage, and still one blanket each."],
	"Sesska's home loom": ["Sesska's small loom, for the work she brings home. There is always work she brings home."],
	"Bolts of bug silk": ["Bolts of silk spun from the mine's bugs, dyed with Evarra's plants. They shimmer when you move."],
	"Thread chest": ["Spools of thread in every colour, sorted by Sesska and then re-sorted by Tikka, by gauge."],
	"Tikka's tinkering bench": ["Tikka's bench at home: a drone with its insides out and a mug of tea gone cold."],
	"Vzz'ket's bedroll": ["A thin bedroll on the bare rock, facing the cavern gate. Vzz'ket says he sleeps with one eye open. He has more than two."],
	"Vzz'ket's kit chest": ["Spare blades, a whetstone, rations and a very old photograph, face down."],
	"Camp stove": ["A little camp stove, still warm. Something is stewing in a dented pot."],
	"Barrels of who-knows-what": ["Sealed barrels with Bram's labels scratched off and relabelled 'LATER'."],
	"Bram's stock shelves": ["Overflow from Bram's shop: rope, fuses, tins and a lot of single boots."],
	"Post boxes": ["Three post boxes: Quill's, labelled neatly, Ix'ali's, dented, and Tar'Besh's, which has a small bell on it."],
	"Residents' notice screen": ["QUIET HOURS AFTER 22:00. - Q.", "Underneath: Sparring is quiet. Mostly. - I."],
	"Spare bed": ["Freya's old room, made up fresh for whoever needs it next."],
	"Guest bed": ["Zaas's old room. He left a towel folded on the end of the bed, just in case."],
	"Sparring mat": ["A worn mat. The scuffs on it show exactly where Ix'ali plants her feet."],
	"Freya's tool cart": ["Freya's tool cart, every drawer labelled, none of the tools in the right drawer."],
	# Rusk's bar (tools/bar.py), 21 Nov. Claude's placeholder lines.
	"Bottle shelves": ["Bottles in six alphabets. Half are empty and kept for the look of the thing."],
	"Rusk's taps": ["Four taps, four kegs. One is labelled 'DO NOT' in Rusk's handwriting. Nobody knows what it is."],
	"Drinks board": ["Today's drinks. Something fast, something slow, something that 'puts hair on your scales'."],
	"Holo-darts": ["A dartboard made of light. Garrick holds the record. Kit says he cheats."],
	"Card table": ["A game of station poker, abandoned mid-hand. Somebody was bluffing."],
	"Open-mic board": ["FRIDAY: OPEN MIC & STORY NIGHT. Under it, in claw marks: 'Vzz'ket goes first.'"],
	"Rusk's mug sign": ["A brass mug on a bracket, polished every morning. It was over the door of his first bar, forty years ago."],
	"Rusk's bed": ["A low fox's bed, a nest of blankets more than a bed. It smells faintly of cedar and spilled ale."],
	"Rusk's tall-tale ledgers": ["Forty years of stories heard across the bar, written down and dated. Some have 'TRUE?' in the margin."],
	"Rusk's sea chest": ["An old spacer's chest with stickers from a dozen ports. Locked, of course."],
	"Kegs": ["Kegs of Rusk's brews, chalk-marked by date."],
	"Supply shelves": ["Glasses, coasters, napkins, and a box marked 'BAR FIGHT SPARES'."],
	"Crates of glasses": ["Spare glasses, packed in straw from the Agri dome."]
}
